[0.006, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Did our signups fall from last month?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 55s over 6 steps, 22,612 tokens, 17 observations gathered, 7 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Cannot be confirmed: no signup or session data exists for the period needed to compare 'this month' against last month, since both PostHog and GA4 data end abruptly on 2026-08-12.  [posthog.event_trend 2e44e016, ga4.get_sessions e34439a1, ga4.get_sessions 3c019cac]\r\n  In the days that are available (Aug 1–12), the daily signup rate was flat around 150–163 per day, showing no sign of decline within that window.  [posthog.event_trend 2e44e016]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  No signup data exists past 2026-08-12  (high)\r\n    - Both PostHog signup events and GA4 ses"]
[0.000, "o", "sions have no recorded data after 2026-08-12, so 'this month' (September) and the second half of August cannot be measured at all.  [posthog.event_trend 2e44e016, posthog.event_trend c1c88e06, ga4.get_sessions e34439a1, ga4.get_sessions 3c019cac]\r\n    - For the days that are covered (2026-08-01 through 2026-08-12), the signup rate was flat, running between 150 and 163 per day with no visible decline.  [posthog.event_trend 2e44e016]\r\n    - HubSpot contact and closed-won records returned no rows for August or September, so they cannot corroborate or contradict a signup change either.  [hubspot.contacts b0f7e32f, hubspot.contacts ca782835, hubspot.closed_won 743de238]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▇▃▅█▂▁▃▇▆▃▃▂|  150 → 163\r\n                        2026-08-01 … 2026-08-12\r\n\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▇▃▅█▂▁▃▇▆▃"]
[0.000, "o", "▃▂|  150 → 163\r\n                        2026-08-01 … 2026-08-12\r\n\r\n  sessions over time\r\n  sessions\r\n    sessions           |▄▁▅▇█▆█▁▃█▆▄▇▅▆▃▂▄▂▄█▃▁▁▂▆▃▃▁█▄▂▁▁▂▆▂▁▅▃█▂▅|  149 → 165\r\n                        2026-07-01 … 2026-08-12\r\n\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The apparent data cutoff at 2026-08-12 across both PostHog and GA4 suggests a sync or pipeline issue on this tenant's connectors rather than an actual absence of signups; this cannot be distinguished from a genuine gap using the tools available.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - PostHog event_trend and GA4 get_sessions both silently truncate results to 2026-08-12 even when a later end_date is requested, without an explicit error — this must be treated as a data gap, not confirmation of no activity.\r\n  - 4 of the 7 c"]
